{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 125, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-to-output edge, connecting node 2 to the output through a conv adds a much-needed extra path, so the gain is larger."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the residual skip where no input-to-output edge exists gains more than swapping it in for an existing conv or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 4 is already absent, killing node 1 removes only the edge 2 path, so the loss is smaller."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 1 is zero, so a conv on edge 4 contributes nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 1 carries no signal, so upgrading edge 2 is ineffective."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 when there is no direct skip leaves the output fed only by edge 4, which hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to an empty edge 3 adds capacity, whereas replacing an existing (often skip) op there loses something useful."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If node 2 is disconnected from the output, operations on edge 1 do not affect the output."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing parameter-free pooling with a conv on the first edge yields a lar